    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25g-perchlike-fishes-7-remaining-groups/plagioscion_squamosissimus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Croakers, also called Drums (Sciaenidae), are a fish family that comprises about 290 species. Most of them are marine, but some occur exclusively in fresh water. In South America about 20 species and 4 genera are known to live in fresh water. The smallest among them becomes only 7 cm long (Pachypops pigmaeus); most become 20-40 cm long. They are quite abundant and important food fish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25g-perchlike-fishes-7-remaining-groups/plagioscion_squamosissimus_en/",
      "html": "<p>However, none of them has been imported as an ornamental fish so far. Now a member of the genus Plagioscion from Peru can be offered for the first time. Probably it is P. squamosissimus, but it may also be the close relative P. auratus. Available size: 8-10 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25g-perchlike-fishes-7-remaining-groups/plagioscion_squamosissimus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Peru.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25g-perchlike-fishes-7-remaining-groups/plagioscion_squamosissimus_en/",
      "html": "<p>P. squamosissimus can reach a length of about 80 cm, whereas P. auratus becomes only half of that.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25g-perchlike-fishes-7-remaining-groups/plagioscion_squamosissimus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Plagioscion are predatory fish and one should not underestimate the broad mouth! Against conspecifics the fish are peaceful.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25g-perchlike-fishes-7-remaining-groups/plagioscion_squamosissimus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Lexicon: Plagioscion: ancient Greek, means “oblique scion” (plagios = oblique, skiaina/“scion” = the common name in Hellenistic Greek for the red mullet). squamosissimus: Latin, the superlative of the adjective meaning “scaled”, so it means something like “with many, many scales”. auratus: Latin, means “golden”.</p><p>Suggested common name: South American silver croaker.</p>"
    }
  ],
